# locksmith
// Pip the Locksmith — authored in YAGE's compact DSL, loaded with `loadCompact`
// (the root entry — no `yaml` dependency). One statement per line; this whole
// file compiles to the SAME validated IR as the eight YAML neighbours, and shares
// the town's storage / functions / commands (gold cell, has_item, give-item).
@ pip Pip the Locksmith #ffb86b

// A declared default, seeded once into the persistent store; it survives plays,
// so the conditional jump below greets a returning customer differently.
declare pip_seen = false

:: start
// Conditional jump: on a return visit (pip_seen persisted) skip the introduction.
-> regreet if: pip_seen
pip happy: Ah, a new face! [b]Welcome[/b] to the workshop. #portrait:pip-smile #line:pip_intro
pip: Locks, keys, picks — if it clicks, I fix it.
set pip_seen = true
-> menu

:: regreet
pip happy: Back already? The bench is always open. #portrait:pip-smile
-> menu

:: menu
? Buy a lockpick (20g) if: gold >= 20 and not has_item('lockpick') -> buy
? Forge a master key if: has_item('master-die') -> bye #disabled
? What's with the east gate? -> gate #once
? Nothing for now -> bye

:: buy
set gold = gold - 20
do give-item id=lockpick
pip happy: One lockpick, [b]sharp[/b] as ever. Mind the tumblers. #portrait:pip-smile
-> menu

:: gate
pip: That old gate to the east? #portrait:pip-think #side:right
The locksmith leans in, voice low. speed=0.6
pip: It wants the [i]rusty key[/i] — and Bron won't part with the lock. #line:pip_gate
-> menu

:: bye
pip happy: Mind how you go. #portrait:pip-smile
end
